/A 38 0 R
/Alt (Three-dimensional model of a protein structure with intertwined magenta and cyan helices and loops. A specific region is highlighted with a red circle, indicating a point of interest. The background is dark, with grid lines.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 28 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
16 0 obj
<<
/A 38 0 R
/Alt (Bar charts and a gel electrophoresis image display mRNA levels. Chart A shows ALG2 mRNA with bars for control, calcium, wild type \(WT\), and mutated samples, with control and mutated having significant differences indicated by asterisks. Chart B shows consistent GAPDH mRNA levels across the same conditions. Panel C presents gel bands for ALG2 and GAPDH mRNA, labeled with sizes in base pairs \(236 and 500\).)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 31 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<<
/A 38 0 R
/Alt ( Bar graphs and a Western blot analyze ALG2 and GAPDH mRNA expression levels under four conditions: control, calcium, WT, and mutant. Graph A shows a significant increase in ALG2 expression in WT and mutant samples. Graph B shows consistent levels of GAPDH across all samples. Graph C shows bands for Alg2 and GAPDH.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 31 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<<
/A 38 0 R
/Alt (Bar graphs and a Western blot image comparing protein levels. Chart A shows alg2 protein levels where control, calcium, and WT samples have higher levels compared to mutated. Chart B depicts gapdh protein, showing consistent levels across all samples. Image C displays alg2 and gapdh bands for control, calcium, WT, and mutated samples, showing differences in band intensity.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 32 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
19 0 obj
<<
/A 38 0 R
/Alt (Bar graphs and Western blot analysis show protein expression levels. Graph A compares alg2 protein across four groups: Control, Calcium, WT, and Mutated, with WT having the highest and Mutated the lowest expression. Graph B shows consistent b-actin protein levels across all groups. Panel C includes corresponding Western blot bands for alg2 and b-actin, with molecular weights of thirty-five and forty-two kilodaltons, respectively.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 32 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
20 0 obj
<<
/A 38 0 R
/Alt (Panel A shows a gel electrophoresis image stained with concanavalin, displaying protein bands for MPM, WT, Control, and Mutated. Panel B shows a similar setup stained with WGA. Panels C and D present bar graphs showing intensity for concanavalin and WGA, respectively, with values for Control, WT, and Mutated. Concanavalin shows higher intensity in Mutated.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 33 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
